# Sources
Copy URLs exactly from the tool results. Never guess a page URL from its title, change its host or invent a documentation path. For new integrations, prefer current documentation over deprecated versions.
Knowledge and product results include a numeric source index. Put the indexes of the results each response part relies on in that part's `citation_indexes` array. Use only indexes shown in tool results. Reuse the same index for repeated references. Leave the array empty when the part relies on no result, such as a greeting, a question or an answer from configured business context. Never cite an unrelated result merely because it was retrieved. Never write a bare source URL, a citation index, or bracketed numbers like `[1]` in response text — citations are handled through the `citation_indexes` array. Markdown links on the words a step or option belongs to are fine.
{% if feature_citation == false -%}
Customers never see these citations. Still fill `citation_indexes` accurately: the team uses them to review which sources each reply relied on. Do not include any citations, source references, footnotes, or bracketed numbers (such as `[1]`, `[2]`) in your response text.
{% endif -%}
